<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 50 0 R
/T (Testing was performed manually using Postman against jsonplaceholder.typicode.com. This involved a structured approach to identify vulnerabilities in the API. Key activities included reconnaissance of endpoints, assessing authentication requirements, and checking for permission validations on user-specific data. Each endpoint was selectively tested to ensure thorough coverage of potential weaknesses. This hands-on method allowed for direct observation of how the API behaves under various inputs and conditions, aiming to uncover security flaws that could be exploited by malicious actors.)
/E (Testing was performed manually using Postman against jsonplaceholder.typicode.com. This involved a structured approach to identify vulnerabilities in the API. Key activities included reconnaissance of endpoints, assessing authentication requirements, and checking for permission validations on user-specific data. Each endpoint was selectively tested to ensure thorough coverage of potential weaknesses. This hands-on method allowed for direct observation of how the API behaves under various inputs and conditions, aiming to uncover security flaws that could be exploited by malicious actors.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
77 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 50 0 R
/T (The methodology also included testing boundary conditions by inputting invalid or out-of-range IDs to assess the API's error handling and response behavior. Detailed inspection of HTTP response headers provided insight into existing security controls, while payload testing on POST endpoints evaluated input validation robustness. The use of Postman's Authorization tab confirmed whether authentication configurations were properly set. This comprehensive approach ensured that each aspect of the API's security posture was evaluated, leading to the identification of several critical vulnerabilities.)
/E (The methodology also included testing boundary conditions by inputting invalid or out-of-range IDs to assess the API's error handling and response behavior. Detailed inspection of HTTP response headers provided insight into existing security controls, while payload testing on POST endpoints evaluated input validation robustness. The use of Postman's Authorization tab confirmed whether authentication configurations were properly set. This comprehensive approach ensured that each aspect of the API's security posture was evaluated, leading to the identification of several critical vulnerabilities.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
